WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:05.069
From HE explosions to molotov infernos, grenade
kills might be rare, but they’re always

00:00:05.069 --> 00:00:06.069
awesome.

00:00:06.069 --> 00:00:11.460
So not including impact kills, here are our
picks for the Top 10 Grenade Kills in CS:GO

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:11.960
History.

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:16.759
Let’s kick off our list with a long-distance
boom — check out roca’s

00:00:16.759 --> 00:00:18.740
throwing arm as he detonates shroud.

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:19.540
Go long!

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:29.340
(Casting)

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:35.480
VP’s carpet bombing of drop room against
Titan takes number nine on the list. Oh,

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:40.300
and the fact that ScreaM accidentally ‘naded
his own team is just the icing on top of the

00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:42.000
high-explosive cake.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:56.080
(Casting)

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:59.660
Pasha’s explosion of Gambit drops in at
number 8.

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:03.000
Perfect timing, perfect camera work and BOOM! Beautiful.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:16.100
(Casting)

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:21.040
It takes some kind of tactical clairvoyance
to ‘nade stack drop on the first round of

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:25.040
a game, but Dignitas did just that in our
pick for number 7.

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:36.180
(Casting)

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:41.480
Pronax’s iconic molly 3k against Cloud9
comes in at number 6 on the list.

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:46.250
Cloud9 might have misplayed the situation
badly, but you can’t deny this play has

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:48.000
lived on in its infamy.

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:59.540
(Casting)

00:01:59.780 --> 00:02:04.220
While the play itself is pretty standard,
Happy’s Defuse-Stopping ‘nade earns number

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:06.990
five because of the stakes in which it happened.

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:11.860
Even in a key round in the finals of a Major,
Happy didn’t miss. Kobe!

00:02:12.020 --> 00:02:20.320
(Casting)

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.700
Want to see a thing of beauty?

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:28.090
Check out this take of A-site Cache by Team
Acer, whose perfect Molotov placements leave

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:30.200
AlienTech no choice but to burn.

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:46.560
(Casting)

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:51.380
Angel’s destruction of e-Frag.net’s 
boost stack is a slam-dunk for number three.

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:55.850
It’s seldom we see three kills with one
‘nade, and the 80 damage on Spyleader is

00:02:55.850 --> 00:02:57.540
just a sweet bonus.

00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:03.320
(Casting)

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:09.080
TaZ’s roasting of TSM takes number two on
the list not only because it’s a great play,

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:11.900
but for the hilarious commentary by James Bardolph.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:27.280
(Casting)

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:33.160
Now for the number one spot on the list, could it
really be anything other than Dosia’s 200

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:36.320
IQ HE ‘nade from the PGL Major?

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:53.960
(Casting)

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:58.040
And those were our picks for the Top
10 Grenade Kills in CS:GO history.

00:03:58.050 --> 00:03:59.340
Did we miss any of your favorites?

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:01.140
Let us know in the comments section below.

